.TH BTOP-THEME-KDE 1 "2026-10-10" "btop-theme-kde" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
btop-theme-kde \- regenerate a btop theme from the active KDE Plasma color scheme
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B btop-theme-kde
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B btop-theme-kde
regenerates a
.BR btop (1)
theme from the active KDE Plasma color scheme and points
.I color_theme
at it in
.IR ~/.config/btop/btop.conf .
.P
It reads the scheme name from
.I ~/.config/kdeglobals
.RB ( General / ColorScheme ),
looks for
.IR <scheme>.colors
in
.I ~/.local/share/color-schemes
then
.IR /usr/share/color-schemes ,
falling back to
.I kdeglobals
itself, and writes
.IR ~/.config/btop/themes/<scheme>.theme .
Safe to run repeatedly: idempotent, a no-op when nothing changed.
.SH OPTIONS
None. There are no command-line flags; environment overrides below are the only inputs.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.I KDE_CONFIG
Path to kdeglobals. Default:
.IR ~/.config/kdeglobals .
.TP
.I BTOP_THEMES_DIR
Theme output directory. Default:
.IR ~/.config/btop/themes .
.TP
.I BTOP_CONF
btop config file updated with
.IR color_theme .
Default:
.IR ~/.config/btop/btop.conf .
.SH EXAMPLES
Run after switching Plasma scheme:
.IP
.EX
btop-theme-kde
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Theme up to date or regenerated.
.TP
.B 1
No active scheme found, or colors could not be parsed.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/kdeglobals
Active scheme name and fallback color definitions.
.TP
.I ~/.config/btop/themes/<scheme>.theme
Generated theme.
.TP
.I ~/.config/btop/btop.conf
Updated with
.IR color_theme="<scheme>" .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR btop (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Written for local use.
